From 71a336dc026ed7d3431e13ea5e8d279075a852e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Han <danielhanchen@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:35:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Studio ROCm: route the FLUX.2 VAE decoder's measured conv
 shapes to a vendored Triton conv2d on gfx1151

Per-shape router (C_in, C_out, kernel, plane bucket, bf16) over the 1x1 and
channel-blocked 3x3 conv2d kernels vendored from ROCm/aiter 6aa39366b7 (MIT).
MIOpen keeps every other call. Variants are built in a background child
(meta-device trace of the default 1024^2 decode at load, cold shapes after a
decode goes quiet), so no decode compiles inline. Linux gfx1151 by default;
UNSLOTH_DIFFUSION_ROCM_TRITON_CONV2D=0 is the kill switch, =1 opts other gfx11
archs and Windows in. Engagement counters in the image status.
